 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Knight. Ghost. Debt. Island. If these words trip people up, it's not their fault.",
   "clip_id": 21941,
   "punch": "NOT THEIR FAULT",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 3.0,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/8174c5b9a1b7fe83.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Start with knight. In Chaucer's day, people really said the K. The sound vanished, but the spelling stayed.",
   "clip_id": 107240,
   "inset_id": 24410,
   "inset_y": 0.4,
   "inset_delay": 0.3,
   "inset_tilt": -5,
   "punch": "K-NIGHT",
   "punch_y": 0.64,
   "punch_delay": 1.8,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/a331ba606d10996b.mp4",
   "inset_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/748ee6b6c0a338c1.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then, in fourteen seventy six, William Caxton brought the printing press to England.",
   "clip_id": 207982,
   "punch": "1476",
   "punch_y": 0.55,
   "punch_delay": 0.9,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/307a814ec8c232a0.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Some of his typesetters were Flemish. And in Flemish spelling, a hard G often came with an H.",
   "clip_id": 1335,
   "punch": "G + H",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 2.6,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/e6223726c844b7a1.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "So the old word gost became ghost. That H simply never left.",
   "clip_id": 2315,
   "items": [
    {
     "emoji": "👻",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.42,
     "size": 0.26,
     "anim": "float",
     "delay": 0.8
    }
   ],
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/7e46ca9cc6ac7063.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Meanwhile, the sounds were moving. That's the Great Vowel Shift.",
   "clip_id": 122232,
   "punch": "VOWEL SHIFT",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 1.6,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/6061aecf27d5eceb.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "In Chaucer's time, bite sounded close to beet. House sounded close to hoose.",
   "clip_id": 202135,
   "items": [
    {
     "emoji": "🏠",
     "x": 0.75,
     "y": 0.34,
     "size": 0.16,
     "anim": "pop",
     "delay": 2.0
    },
    {
     "emoji": "👄",
     "x": 0.25,
     "y": 0.34,
     "size": 0.16,
     "anim": "pop",
     "delay": 0.8
    }
   ],
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/2c12e6b853210945.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "The sounds changed, but the letters mostly didn't.",
   "clip_id": 51756,
   "punch": "OLD SPEECH",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 1.6,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/90d11017fa761954.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then, in the fifteen hundreds, scholars added letters to make words look like Latin.",
   "clip_id": 113483,
   "inset_id": 250772,
   "inset_y": 0.42,
   "inset_delay": 0.8,
   "inset_tilt": 4,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/852b082882aac884.mp4",
   "inset_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/7bbb406af8ad2b93.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "Dette became debt, with a silent B, just to match the Latin word debitum.",
   "clip_id": 49919,
   "punch": "SILENT B",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 1.4,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/50da46bca86f32c4.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "And here's the best one. The S in island is a mistake.",
   "clip_id": 2946,
   "items": [
    {
     "emoji": "🏝️",
     "x": 0.5,
     "y": 0.42,
     "size": 0.22,
     "anim": "pop",
     "delay": 0.4
    }
   ],
   "punch": "MISTAKE",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 1.8,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/d495f06d7c19170c.mp4"
  },
  {
   "say": "It was added to link it to Latin insula. But island comes from Old English.",
   "clip_id": 344380,
   "punch": "WRONG ROOT",
   "punch_y": 0.66,
   "punch_delay": 2.2,
   "clip_path": "/root/.cache/shorts_clips/26ea6f754d8644d1.mp4"
  },
  {
